{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghZH7Ei8QHcWMtFa3BGr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fitting the three bands as low‑spin d⁵ (ground term ²T₂g) with C = 4.6 B gives **Dq ≈ 2716 cm⁻¹ (Δ ≈ 27 160 cm⁻¹)** and **B ≈ 877 cm⁻¹**, with C ≈ 4040 cm⁻¹.\n\n**Method.** I used the Tanabe–Sugano fitting tool, pinned to the low‑spin side.\n\n**Fixing C.** The tool takes C as an absolute value, not as a ratio. My first fit used its default C = 3850 cm⁻¹, which gave B ≈ 878 cm⁻¹. That implies C/B ≈ 4.4, not 4.6. I refit with C = 4040 cm⁻¹ (4.6 × 877). The result was B = 876.6 cm⁻¹, so C/B = 4.61, which is self‑consistent.\n\n**Assignments.** The three bands are transitions from ²T₂g to excited doublets:\n\n| Observed (cm⁻¹) | Calculated (cm⁻¹) | Assignment |\n|---|---|---|\n| 22 640 | 22 639 | ²T₂g → ²A₂g |\n| 22 930 | 22 931 | ²T₂g → ²T₁g |\n| 25 080 | 25 080 | ²T₂g → ²T₂g(b) |\n\nThe residuals are under 1 cm⁻¹. The ²T₂g → ²Eg band is predicted at about 27 200 cm⁻¹.\n\n{\"Dq\": 2716, \"B\": 877, \"C\": 4040, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Low-spin d5 fit of three doublet bands with C fixed at 4.6B gives Dq≈2716 and B≈877 cm^-1 with sub-cm^-1 residuals.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2776,"cache_read_input_tokens":10957,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2776,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3376a6c2-7c40-4ecf-a5d7-aba173f79c3d","uuid":"0590b135-e65f-4b91-aa46-5e8819a86c17","timestamp":"2026-11-04T08:17:01.950Z","request_id":"req_011CghZH6sPc5CghmSoP4B12"}
